id: pm-gh1606
title: "GH-1606: Validate public SDK runtime operand values before mutation internals"
description: "**Version:** `@unbrained/pm-cli` 2026.10.26 SDK (`@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk`), Node 24.19.0.\n\n**Repro** (`node --experimental-strip-types x.ts`):\n```ts\nimport { PmClient } from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk';\nconst pm = new PmClient({ pmRoot: '.agents/pm', author: 'agent' });\nawait pm.append('pm-xxxx', { text: 'object not string' } as any);\n```\n**Observed:** uncaught `TypeError: a.trim is not a function` with a minified bundle excerpt — 7,414 bytes of stderr, no error code, and nothing naming `append`'s body operand. Catching it yields only the bare TypeError. Updating with a numeric `estimatedMinutes: 2` likewise throws `TypeError: e.trim is not a function` (the string `'2'` works).\n\n**Expected:** public SDK methods validate positional/option value types at the boundary and throw a typed `PmCliError` (usage code) naming the operand, the expected type and a short corrective example (e.g. \"append body must be a string; use comments(id, { add }) for a comment\").\n\n**Why it matters for agents:** agents and tool/JSON bridges call the SDK with dynamically built values, so TypeScript types do not protect them. A minified TypeError forces the agent to inspect bundled internals to fix a simple call-shape mistake. (Related but different: #1520 is about unknown option keys being dropped.)\n\n\nIntake boundary: this is a report against published 2026.10.26, not proof of a current-checkout defect. Reproduce in an external sandbox before implementation. Related completed work retains its shipped scope. Proposed examples or categories are not accepted contracts until validated.\n\nSource: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1606"
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: agent-ux,github,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-26T19:02:10.791Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T14:50:38.930Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-28T14:47:46.298Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-28T14:47:46.298Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Native public-client controls cover an object append operand and numeric estimatedMinutes according to the published input contract, alongside valid corresponding values.; Errors identify the public method, operand, expected type and corrective example through PmCliError usage semantics; rejected calls leave documents, history and receipts unchanged.; Validation derives from SDK-owned contracts across convenience methods and JSON bridges, preserving completed unknown-key and bulk-duration guards without mirrored per-wrapper schemas or a global exception handler."
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "SDK and client mutation operands and contract-declared options now reject malformed values with typed usage errors before coercion, transport resolution or writes. Shared update/reopen ID guards and recurrence-reason validation prevent raw TypeErrors and partial reopen mutations."
expected_result: "Malformed native or client calls identify the offending operand or field with invalid_argument_value and changed:false while preserving item and history bytes; valid calls remain usable."
actual_result: "All four linked groups pass; all 11,519 source tests pass with exact 100% coverage and three platform skips. Real npm/Node24 and Bun packed consumers pass fourteen typed no-write controls, both public entrypoints and npx/bunx. Typecheck, graph, record integrity, secrets and bounded mutation checks pass. Qualified local timing failures remain preserved; exact-head hosted checks and renewed review remain merge gates."
